# L §5.14.1 next(K, d): "the first movement of event kind K whose day is on or after d (first(m in K over d ..) ties
# by m.day) ... When none is planned yet, its binding is empty at the cut and its span reaches past it, so it is a hole
# naming the binding (HOLE-NOTYET, §3.1)"; L §8.1 HOLE-NOTYET "<x>: no <event> yet, and its span reaches past the cut"
# (writer 8: x is the binding's variable, m in the stated equivalence; was pending, removed by the review).  wage[m] for m in pay_months (2026-01..2026-06) falls on day_of(m, 10) (L §4.2): on or after
# 2026-03-10 the first is wage[2026-03], on or after 2026-03-11 wage[2026-04] on 2026-04-10; after the last
# (2026-06-10) none is planned: HOLE-NOTYET.  L §5.10 "Kind and unit are read by x in K and unit(x)": konto is a place
# of unit PLN.
=== m.tally
model n
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index pay_months = month 2026-01..2026-06

kind wages: event certain
  leg cash: PLN

input pay_dom: int
input pay_amt: money PLN

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move wage[m in pay_months]: wages
  on day_of(m, pay_dom)
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay_amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  pay_dom = 10
  pay_amt = 4 000.00 PLN

ask n1: next(wages, 2026-03-10), next(wages, 2026-03-11)
ask n2: next(wages, 2026-03-11).day
ask n3: next(wages, 2026-06-11)
ask u1: unit(konto)
=== expect
n1: (wage[2026-03], wage[2026-04])
  cut 2026-01-01
n2: 2026-04-10
  cut 2026-01-01
n3: ?"m: no wages yet, and its span reaches past the cut" (wages)
  cut 2026-01-01
u1: PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
